## Interface: 11509, 20506, 16001
## Title: Spoken Zones
## Notes: Zone and subzone lore on the world map, read aloud through the Spoken player. Formerly ZoneLore.
## Notes-deDE: Zonen- und Gebietslore auf der Weltkarte, vorgelesen durch den Spoken-Player. Ehemals ZoneLore.
## Notes-esES: Historia de zonas y subzonas en el mapa del mundo, leída en voz alta a través del reproductor Spoken. Anteriormente ZoneLore.
## Notes-esMX: Historia de zonas y subzonas en el mapa del mundo, leída en voz alta a través del reproductor Spoken. Anteriormente ZoneLore.
## Notes-frFR: Histoire des zones et sous-zones sur la carte du monde, lue à voix haute grâce au lecteur Spoken. Anciennement ZoneLore.
## Notes-ptBR: História de zonas e subzonas no mapa do mundo, lida em voz alta através do reprodutor Spoken. Anteriormente ZoneLore.
## Notes-ruRU: История зон и подзон на карте мира, озвученная через проигрыватель Spoken. Ранее — ZoneLore.
## Notes-koKR: Spoken 플레이어로 월드맵의 지역과 하위 지역 전승을 소리내어 읽습니다. 이전 이름은 ZoneLore.
## Notes-zhCN: 在世界地图上通过 Spoken 播放器朗读区域和次级区域传说。前身为 ZoneLore。
## Notes-zhTW: 在世界地圖上透過 Spoken 播放器朗讀區域和次級區域傳說。前身為 ZoneLore。
## Version: 2.2.1
## Author: rusty
## SavedVariables: SpokenZonesDB
## SavedVariablesPerCharacter: SpokenZonesCharDB
# ZoneLoreDB, ZoneLoreCharDB and ZoneLoreQueueDB -- the addon's variables under its old
# name -- are declared by the ZoneLore tombstone folder, which is what keeps that file
# loading. Migration.lua copies them once; the Spoken player reads ZoneLoreQueueDB itself.
## LoadSavedVariablesFirst: true
# ^ load-bearing beyond convenience: the generated data files under Data/ ask
# Language.lua which language to build a table for, and it can only answer that
# early because ZoneLoreDB is already populated. Without this line every player
# silently reads English.
## OptionalDeps: SpokenPlayer, ZoneLore, SpokenZonesAudio, ZoneLoreAudio, ZoneLoreAudio64
# Spoken is the player this addon speaks through. Optional here so a hand-installed
# copy without it loads and says what is missing rather than failing to load at
# all; addon managers install it from the CurseForge dependency. The packs are not
# a registration mechanism either -- they register themselves into SpokenZonesAudioPacks
# and Audio.lua walks that on demand -- so this list is load order only.
#
# Both pack folder names are listed: SpokenZonesAudio is what ships now, ZoneLoreAudio
# what a player installed before the rename, and ZoneLoreAudio64 the retired smaller
# tier. A name here that nobody has installed costs nothing.
## IconTexture: Interface\AddOns\SpokenZones\Textures\AddonIcon.tga
## X-License: Addon code MIT. Zone lore text from warcraft.wiki.gg, CC BY-SA 4.0.
## X-Credits: Lore text sourced from warcraft.wiki.gg contributors (CC BY-SA 4.0).

